{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Do not be.</b> If you prayed from morning until evening and fasted and the like, you will be desolate (תשומם), and the meaning is: you will turn aside from the way of settlement, as the Romiti [Christians?] do in the land of Edom and Ishmael. And likewise if you sought to be wise more than enough. And the word תשומם is from the nif'al binyan. Some say that the dagesh in the shin is not due to a missing nun of nif'al, but rather due to a missing tav of hitpa'el, and it should have been תשתומם. For a nif'al of doubled [root-letter] verbs in which both [letters] are present is not found; rather it is found in the hitpa'el binyan of verbs whose ayin is not whole [i.e., guttural], like תבנה and תכונן."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The reading הר\"ומיטי is uncertain; tentatively resolved as 'the Romiti,' apparently referring to a group in Christian or Islamic lands. The grammatical argument is rendered hyper-literally; the syntax is compressed and the final clause is elliptic in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:10.634328994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}